      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Thirty-two patients were treated with placebo tablets or indomethacin (25 mg three times daily) in a six-month, double-blind, cross-over trial. During indomethacin therapy, 75 per cent of patients experienced significant pain relief while associated vomiting and diarrhoea were relieved in 44 per cent and 64 per cent of patients respectively. The efficacy of indomethacin was comparable to that of other prostaglandin synthetase inhibitors."},
